    "created_at": "2024-08-05T22:20:05Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-08-05T22:21:20Z",
    "body": "> https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/10537#issuecomment-2269896218\r\n\r\n@tabatkins, how is a checkbox by definition unchecked? Isn't that merely a matter of convention? It seems feasible that an implementation could default to a checked state. For any attribute, surely having its opposite is solely an advantage, since it makes changing defaults easier, and makes authors more confident that were a default to change, it wouldn't impact them.",
